Option A: `pay` restructures: first get/apply receipt once (ledger.apply is idempotent), then retry only the acknowledge in a separate loop, forwarding the same receipt. Ledger.apply idempotency handles the "duplicate debit" case for concurrent calls / repeated pay calls with same key.

Option B: keep the loop that calls ledger.apply then acknowledge, relying on ledger idempotency so a re-apply returns the same receipt. "Forwarding the same receipt each time" then holds because ledger returns the same receipt object.

The check: "Retry only Transient, up to attempts total tries, forwarding the same receipt each time." Both interpretations satisfy "same receipt each time" under Option B as long as the ledger returns the same receipt object. Hmm, but under Option B, each retry re-computes receipt from ledger. Under Option A, we capture the receipt once and retry acknowledge only.

